| 7 | Judul ditetapkan sebagai usulan (14 kata Indonesia, 13 kata Inggris): "Melanjutkan atau Menghentikan *Scrolling*: Pengalaman Mahasiswa ketika Jeda Belajar dengan Video Pendek Melampaui Niat" dan "Keep Scrolling or Stop: Students' Experiences When Short-Video Study Breaks Exceed Their Intentions". Kelompok dapat menggantinya | berkas kanonik |
| 8 | Posisi teori ditempatkan di 2c (penutup), pembenaran hermeneutik di 3a, prosedur keterbukaan di 3d. Kalimat "tanpa diperlakukan sebagai kategori yang pasti muncul" di 2b dan penyangkalan kausalitas dan adiksi di 3a (pengulangan tujuan) dihapus | `Tinjauan pustaka.working.md`, `Metode.working.md` |


FILE: review-triage.md
# Triage: external review 1 (codex gpt-6-astra, low), 20 Oktober 2026

Scope: 2a and 2d plus reference list. Findings in `review-findings.md`, prompt in `review-prompt.md`, run log in `review-run.log` (exit 0).

| # | Finding | Verdict | Evidence | Section |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | Novelty claim ignores Hossain et al. (2024) | Valid | Hossain transcript PDF p. 22: awareness of time spent on SM is a cue that "snapped them out of procrastination". P13: TikTok covers the clock, "suddenly you've spent half an hour". So the overrun moment is partly documented. What Hossain does not follow is the decision to keep scrolling after that awareness. "belum tercakup" in 2d manfaat is too strong. "paling sedikit dipahami" in 2a para 4 is the writer's framing, defensible but safer softened. | 2d (main), 2a para 4 (optional) |
