passive, and letting it happen.

# Consuming alcohol (or taking other drugs) is subject

to a similar analysis. Despite the undeniable addictive- ness of alcohol, and despite popular images that many people cannot control their drinking, it is clear that most people who drink alcohol are actively acquiescing in the process. Ordering or pouring a drink and raising a glass to one's lips are deliberate, volitional acts. Binge eaters likewise often describe their eating as out of control, yet in many cases the person must acquiesce to

