# response is often a matter of deliberate action. Outside

the laboratory, failures to delay gratification may often involve even more extensive and obvious forms of active acquiescence (e.g., when the person drops out of college or empties a savings account). There are of course instances in which the person's acquiescence is even more extreme. People do some- times seem to arrange to lose control. Marlatt (1985)

