# thwart their own self-regulatory programs.

Apart from such extreme cases, it would usually be inappropriate to say that the person planned and engi- neered the entire scenario in advance; in fact, the person may often be quite chagrined by the eventual outcome. To simply say that the self-regulation failures reflect deliberate free choice would therefore be somewhat misleading. On the other hand, the stereotype of the helpless, passive victim overwhelmed against his or her will by uncontrollable impulses is not accurate either. The person did participate, more or less freely and

